-- title:
--   Finite-map data of large degree invertible in R
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative local Noetherian ring, let $C$ be a scheme and let $c \colon C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ be a proper morphism which is smooth of relative dimension $1$ and satisfies `GeometricallyIntegral`; let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$, that is a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ whose composite with $c$ is the identity; let $\mathcal V$ be a `TwoAffineOpenCover` of $C$, i.e. two affine opens $U_0, U_1$ with $U_0 \sqcup U_1 = \top$ and with $U_0 \sqcap U_1$ affine; and let $m_0$ be a natural number. The assertion is that there is a `FiniteMapData` $\mathfrak F$ for the pair $(c,\varepsilon)$ with $m_0 \le \mathfrak F.m$ and with the image of $\mathfrak F.m$ in $R$ a unit. Such a datum consists of opens $U, V \subseteq C$, sections $f \in \Gamma(C,U)$ and $g \in \Gamma(C,V)$, and a natural number $m$, subject to: $U$ and $V$ are affine open and $U \sqcup V = \top$; a point of $C$ lies in $U$ exactly when it is not in the set-theoretic image of $\varepsilon$; $U \sqcap V$ equals both the basic open set of $f$ and that of $g$; the restrictions of $f$ and $g$ to $U \sqcap V$ have product $1$; with the $R$-algebra structures on $\Gamma(C,U)$ and $\Gamma(C,V)$ induced by $c$, the evaluation maps $R[X] \to \Gamma(C,U)$, $X \mapsto f$, and $R[X] \to \Gamma(C,V)$, $X \mapsto g$, are finite ring maps; and for every local $R$-algebra $S$ and every $s \in S$ the quotient $S \otimes_R \Gamma(C,U)$ by the ideal generated by $1 \otimes f - s \otimes 1$ is a finite free $S$-module of rank $m$.
--
--   This is the chart-wise form of the existence, on a proper smooth geometrically integral relative curve with a section, of a finite morphism to $\mathbb P^1_R$ of degree $m \ge m_0$ prime to the residue characteristic, with the pole divisor supported on the section: $U$ is the complement of $\varepsilon$, $f$ is the affine coordinate and $g = 1/f$. It is the version in which a cover of $C$ by two affine opens with affine intersection is assumed, and it feeds the unconditional statement [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_finiteMapData_le_isUnit`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_finiteMapData_le_isUnit) as well as the construction of relative Picard data in `AlgebraicGeometry.RelPicard`.
